 versions of our site every day and we do  it with the power of the data that we  are gathering from all of the disparate  data sources trying to understand you  know what do our customers like what are  their preferences and and we really hear  from them and learn from them and then  take those learnings to drive their  future experiences so in this case I  have the same day same time there are  three different customers who came to  this a lily site on your left  extreme left is a customer who buys  apparel and fitness gear and the middle  was a shopper who came through Footwear  advertisement and landed on on our site  and on the extreme right is a customer  who predominantly buys for her kids and  home goods so you can see the the  experience is radically different for  all of our customers and this is key to  driving engagement right this goes back  to by doing all of that we were able to  get to 91% of our orders today are  actually coming from repeat customers we  have over 6.1 million active customers  today our number of active customers has  grown 25 24 percent year-over-year or  revenues at the end of q1 had drawn 17  percent year-over-year currently we are  at 1.6 billion dollars and one of the  things I want to mention I mentioned  this in the context of the data platform  itself is the data lives in Google Cloud  storage right  we are gathering all of the data but  even to power the machine learning and  personalization experience we are  actually leveraging the the Hadoop spark  ecosystem the data proc clusters that  Google has to offer and using that we  are creating all the features that we  need to drive the personalization  experience and again depending on what  kind of features we are building what  kind of transformations the cadence will  vary some are near real-time some are  you know every half hour every day and  so forth  one of the other interesting challenges  here is people who work you know  familiar with the machine learning  personalization recommendation systems  play space is there is an inherent rip  you know presentation bias and in  machine learning joggin and what does  that mean that means is if a customer  never sees a product they're never going  to click on it if they never click into  it they're never going to buy it right  so one of the places where we use Google  Cloud Storage was also to address that  problem of presentation-wise how do we  bring transparency into what we do and  how we do and share it with our business  partners so they understand what is the  exposure that personalization is driving  through the customer base and we did  that by having all of our logs so when  we are serving by the way these are  served in near-real-time right so as we  are solving these experiences to  customers based on their latest and  greatest data we are actually logging  those experiences and we make those logs  available in GCS which helps us to  actually mind those logs after the fact  or him during the course of the day at  periodic intervals and be able to  present reports and dashboards to all  four partners telling them how  personalization is actually driving  exposure from our customers on the  products that they care about which was  very insightful as well  so I mentioned briefly how it works you  know we're launching millions of sites  every day we receive all of that data we  process that data this is where Google  Cloud Storage comes into the picture we  are using data Pro cluster to train our  machine learning models based on the  features that we are deriving from that  data and we're using that to inform the  future experiences for our customers  it drives higher revenue engagement but  above all it makes our customers happy  so there are other places where we are  actually using or my partners and on the  marketing side are actually using that  data to actually figure out what the  customer lifetime value is and and they  do that by really looking at that data  again and 